{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS7vxgzU7XqugKzvKczC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the generator, but I haven't pushed anything, so it's untested on the API and the watch. Whether the watch now shows the planned ranges is still unconfirmed.\n\n**What was wrong:** `gen.py` wrote each HR range as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": 68, \"end\": 75}`. As far as I know Intervals.icu's workout format, a range is written as `start` and `end`, while `value` means a single target. So Intervals most likely treated each step as one %LTHR number and ignored `end`. It then sent that single number to Garmin as a heart-rate zone, and the watch drew the edges of its own zone. That matches what you saw: changing the watch's LTHR moved the bands, but you never got 151–160. The API returning the event exactly as sent only shows the fields were valid JSON, not that they were read as a range. I couldn't check the format against the live API here; it's based on my knowledge of how Intervals encodes ranges.\n\n**What I changed in `hr_target` in `gen.py`:**\n- A range is now written as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. Intervals should convert that using the LTHR of 172 and export it as a bpm range, e.g. Tempo 88–93% → about 151–160.\n- If the low and high values are equal, it writes a single `value`.\n- If the low value is above the high one, it stops with an error.\n\nThe plan files and `push.sh` are unchanged. I ran the generator on `plans/tempo-run.json` and the output has the new `start`/`end` form.\n\n**To confirm it works:** regenerate `event.json`, push it, sync the watch, and check that Tempo shows about 151–160 and Float about 129–141. If they still show as zones, check whether Intervals' Garmin export settings force HR targets into zones; I'm not sure such a setting exists.\n\nEverything above is also written up in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":24313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":774},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cde443fa-b71f-4bc2-8d58-acbbbfc004ad","uuid":"b902f34b-e997-4d10-ad8b-4c55be5226c3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:35:45.039Z","request_id":"req_011CgS7vxEx5xCycu662V82R"}
